  "id": "DrugBank_DB01095 - MONDO_5311",
  "verbalization": "Fluvastatin is implicated in the pathogenesis of atherosclerosis through a multi-step pathway that involves the treatment of arteriosclerosis disorder. The evidence suggests that Fluvastatin, through its indication for arteriosclerosis disorder, is linked to the development of atherosclerosis via the actions of related drugs such as alirocumab, rosuvastatin, and atorvastatin. These drugs, in turn, are indicated for arteriosclerosis disorder and are known to reduce atherosclerosis risk by modulating lipid metabolism and inflammatory processes. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential mechanism by which Fluvastatin may contribute to the prevention of atherosclerosis, particularly through its role in targeting the underlying disorder. The evidence supports a direct relationship between Fluvastatin and atherosclerosis, mediated through the treatment of arteriosclerosis disorder, and underscores the importance of considering these indirect pathways in drug repurposing efforts.",
